  "notes": "GOV-style plain-language Medicaid plan chooser. Distinctive: the comparison is personalised to the household's actual doctors, child's inhaler and pharmacy, with per-person tags (Angela / Mateo) on each row and consequence text in cells ('Mateo would need a different pulmonologist'). Tri-state legend (covered / covered with a catch / not covered) uses filled circle check, amber triangle, red x plus pink/amber cell tints. The default auto-assigned plan is flagged in both a top warning banner and a pill on its column. Choosing a plan tints the entire column teal and fills the button; a sticky bottom 'Your selection' bar reports the choice and enables Review and submit. Deadline cell in summary strip highlighted amber with '15 days left'."
